@page "/no-access"
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "No access"; var me = User.CurrentStaff(); }
<h1>You do not have access to this page</h1>
@if (me is null || me.Roles.Count == 0)
{
  <p>You signed in@(me is null ? "" : $" as {me.Account}"), but your account is not in any of the portal's groups.</p>
}
else
{
  <p>Your account can do other things in the portal, but not this.</p>
}
<p>Access comes from Active Directory groups, one for each role:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Coordinator</strong>: works the queue, assigns requests, asks providers for missing information.</li>
  <li><strong>Licensed clinician</strong>: decides prior authorization requests.</li>
  <li><strong>Physician</strong>: decides any request, and is the only role that decides concurrent reviews.</li>
  <li><strong>Admin</strong>: registers and switches off provider systems.</li>
</ul>
<p>Ask your supervisor to have IT add you to the right group, then sign out of Windows and back in.</p>
